---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import DocSection from '../components/DocSection.astro';
import DocContact from '../components/DocContact.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const contents = [
  { href: '#does', text: 'What Holiplanz does' },
  { href: '#check', text: 'Check before you book' },
  { href: '#account', text: 'Your account' },
  { href: '#payment', text: 'Plans and payment' },
  { href: '#fair', text: 'Using it fairly' },
  { href: '#owns', text: 'Who owns what' },
  { href: '#limits', text: 'Our responsibility' },
];

const plans = [
  { term: 'First journey', value: 'Free, every feature, once' },
  { term: 'Trip Pass — $19', value: 'One trip · does not auto-renew' },
  { term: 'Premium — $49', value: 'Yearly · renews until cancelled' },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of use — Holiplanz"
  description="Holiplanz is a planning tool, not a travel agent — it books nothing. What we do, what to check before you book, and how plans and payment work."
  heading="Terms of use"
  draftNote="The liability and refund clauses in particular need a lawyer's eye."
>
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    We plan trips, you book them. Use the app sensibly, check the details before you commit money,
    and either of us can walk away.
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="rail">
    {contents.map((item) => <a href={item.href}>{item.text}</a>)}
  </Fragment>

  <DocSection id="does" heading="What Holiplanz does">
    <p>
      We draft travel itineraries and suggest places to stay and things to do. We are a planning
      tool, not a travel agent, tour operator or booking platform. We don't reserve anything, take
      payment for travel, or act as your agent with any hotel, airline or venue.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  {/*
    Set apart deliberately: this is the one clause that stops a traveller acting
    on a wrong itinerary, so it must not read like the others.
  */}
  <DocSection id="check" heading="Check before you book" callout>
    <p>
      Plans are generated automatically and can be wrong. Opening hours change, places close,
      prices move, and routes that look walkable on a map sometimes aren't. Always confirm the
      details with the provider before you spend money or rely on them — especially anything
      involving visas, health requirements, or safety.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection id="account" heading="Your account">
    <p>
      You need to be an adult to hold an account, and you're responsible for what happens under it.
      Keep your login to yourself.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection id="payment" heading="Plans and payment">
    <div class="doc__rows">
      {
        plans.map((plan) => (
          <div class="doc__row doc__row--tight">
            <span class="doc__rowTerm">{plan.term}</span>
            <span class="doc__rowValue">{plan.value}</span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p>
      Your first journey is free, with every feature unlocked once. After that a Trip Pass is a
      one-time payment covering a single trip and does not auto-renew; Premium is an annual
      subscription that does, until you cancel. Payment is handled by the App Store or Google Play,
      so their billing and refund rules apply alongside ours.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection id="fair" heading="Using it fairly">
    <p>
      Don't scrape the service, resell the plans it produces as your own product, try to break its
      limits, or use it for anything unlawful. We may suspend accounts that do.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection id="owns" heading="Who owns what">
    <p>
      The app, its design and the Holiplanz name are ours. Your trips and your Trip Passport are
      yours — we only use them to run the service for you.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection id="limits" heading="Where our responsibility ends">
    <p>
      We take care with the service but can't promise a plan will be complete, current or suited to
      your circumstances. We aren't responsible for third-party providers you book with, or for
      losses arising from relying on a suggestion without checking it. Nothing here limits rights
      you have under consumer law that can't be limited.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="Ending it">
    <p>
      You can close your account whenever you like. We may end or suspend access if these terms are
      broken, or if we stop offering the service — in which case we'll give reasonable notice.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection heading="Changes">
    <p>
      If we change these terms materially we'll tell you in the app before the change takes effect.
    </p>
  </DocSection>

  <DocContact label="Questions about these terms" email={site.generalEmail} />
</LegalPage>
